      <div class="note about">Over-the-air digital TV (ATSC 1.0), receive only. Stations are found by their pilot, 309 kHz above the bottom of each 6 MHz channel. With a HackRF the whole channel is sampled at 8 MS/s and decoded in bursts through the 8VSB equalizer and trellis decoder, Reed-Solomon, the transport stream and PSIP (the channel list, the program guide, the station clock), with a picture from each subchannel's MPEG-2 video. The CPU decodes what it can and skips the rest. The tables and pictures repeat, so every view still fills in, and the share decoded is shown. AUTO steps through VHF 2\u201313 and UHF 14\u201336 and stays on each station until its channels, pictures and guide are in. Everything heard is kept. Tap a subchannel for its guide, its streams and the raw tables.</div>
